Subject: [PATCH] WebRTC: use the negotiated MID when incoming caps omit it

GStreamer 1.24 webrtcbin src caps can omit a-mid. An empty MID makes
connectIncomingTrack create a duplicate receiver instead of activating
the receiver delivered by ontrack. Its original track stays muted even
though RTP arrives and video decodes. Fall back to the transceiver MID
when the caps do not provide one; preserve explicit RTP caps MIDs.

--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerIncomingTrackProcessor.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerIncomingTrackProcessor.cpp
@@ -81,4 +81,9 @@
-
+
     g_object_get(m_pad.get(), "transceiver", &m_data.transceiver.outPtr(), nullptr);
+    if (m_data.mid.isEmpty()) {
+        GUniqueOutPtr<char> mid;
+        g_object_get(m_data.transceiver.get(), "mid", &mid.outPtr(), nullptr);
+        m_data.mid = String::fromUTF8(mid.get());
+    }
-
+
     if (auto msIdAttribute = gstStructureGetString(structure, "a-msid"_s)) {
